SUMMARY:PSU Theater Arts presents: As You Like It
DESCRIPTION:Love\, disguise\, and transformation take center stage in Shakespeare’s classic romantic comedy reimagined in the context of Queer joy. Join us in the Forest of Arden for a playful\, poetic escape. \nShowtimes: \nThursday\, May 21\, 7:30 PM (Preview – $15 tickets available)\nFriday\, May 22\, 7:30 PM (Opening night! Join us for a post-show reception with the company.)\nSaturday\, May 23\, 7:30 PM\nSunday\, May 24\, 2:00 PM (Followed by a free improvisation performance by the PSU Impro Ensemble at 4:30 PM: Post-Show Unscripted) \nWednesday\, May 27\, 7:30 PM (Community night: Arts workers\, PSU community and alumni receive $10 tickets)\nThursday\, May 28\, 7:30 PM\nFriday\, May 29\, 7:30 PM\nSaturday\, May 30\, 2:00 PM \nDuration: This performance is approximately 2 hours and 15 minutes long\, including an intermission. \nEditor’s note: This event is a community submission.
URL:https://pdxparent.com/event-single/psu-theater-arts-presents-as-you-like-it/2026-05-24/
LOCATION:Lincoln Performance Hall at Portland State University\, 1620 SW Park at Market
CATEGORIES:Inclusive,Kids Calendar,LGBTQ+,Music,Theater
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://pdxparent.com/wp-content/uploads/10-1080x1080-Broadcasting-Square.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Portland State Theater Arts":MAILTO:music@pdx.edu
END:VEVENT
